    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d148-a47">

                <pb facs="0441" n="319" xml:id="pg319"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure G 5.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Apia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1882-04-01"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">April</hi> 1, 1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Augustus Nelson</hi>:</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to inform you Haupt-Agentur der
                    deutschen Handelsund Plantagen-Gesellsch. der Südsee-Inseln zu Hamburg August
                    Godefroy have lodged a complaint through the Kaiserlich Deutsches Konsulat für
                    die Südsee-Inseln in this consulate against you for selling fire-arms and
                    ammunition in Savaii, contrary to laws of the King and Government of Samoa dated
                    the 25th day of October, A. D. 1880.</p>
                <p>You will, therefore, please call at this consulate this day to answer to the
                    above charge.</p>
                <p>I have honor to be. sir,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. E. VARICK ALVORD,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting United
                            States Vice-Consul</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
